# What must never reach a build context, and therefore never reach a layer.
#
# The first block is the one that matters: an `.env` copied into the builder
# stage is in that stage's filesystem for ever, and `docker history` and
# `docker save` both hand it to anybody with the image. `COPY . .` in the
# Dockerfile is what makes this file load-bearing rather than a tidiness
# measure, and tests/deploy.test.mjs asserts these lines are here.

# --- credentials -----------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.local
.env.production
.env.*.local
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/id_ed25519*
**/id_rsa*
secrets/

# --- git, which carries every version of every file above -------------------
.git
.github
.gitignore

# --- things the build makes for itself --------------------------------------
node_modules
.next
out
build
dist
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- things no server needs ------------------------------------------------
docs
design
research
eval/results
eval/recordings
tests
db/test
db/seed
db/.data
server
*.log
*.pdf
README.md
